# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HealThaali — security and caching headers
#
# Both Cloudflare Pages and Netlify read a file named `_headers` from the
# publish root. Astro copies everything in `public/` into `dist/`, so this file
# ships as `dist/_headers` automatically — no extra build step.
#
# Vercel does NOT read `_headers`; `vercel.json` mirrors these same rules. If you
# change one, change the other.
#
# ── Why the CSP looks like this ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# `script-src 'unsafe-inline'` is required, not laziness:
#   * the theme boot script in BaseLayout runs before the first paint so dark
#     mode never flashes white — a nonce or a separate file would defeat that;
#   * the JSON-LD blocks on /, /features, /about and the rest are inline.
# `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` is required because Astro inlines small
# stylesheets into the HTML.
# `static.cloudflareinsights.com` is only used when PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ID is set.
#
# `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com` exists so a blog post can embed a
# recipe video. The host is YouTube's privacy-preserving player origin, and it is
# the ONLY frame this site allows. The player is not requested on page load:
# a post renders a button, and the <iframe> is created from script when someone
# presses it (see the click-to-play note in src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro).
#
# `form-action` is deliberately NOT set. The contact form posts to
# PUBLIC_CONTACT_ENDPOINT, which does not exist yet, so any value here would be a
# guess that could silently break the form. Once the endpoint is real, add THIS
# line inside the `/*` block below to lock it down:
#
#   form-action 'self' https://your-form-endpoint.example
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# Astro fingerprints everything in _astro/ (name includes a content hash), so
# these can be cached forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Unfingerprinted public files: a week is plenty, and short enough that a logo
# or favicon swap is picked up without renaming the file.
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/favicon-32.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/icon-192.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/icon-512.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/og-image.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# These describe the deploy itself, so keep them short.
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/sitemap-index.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
